--- !u!114 &3559007171211044604
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 1
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 935228c0fd2628c4db5028980babef0b, type: 3}
  m_Name: NarrativeParagraph
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Tutorials.Editor::Unity.Tutorials.Editor.Paragraphs.NarrativeParagraph
  m_MaskingSettings:
    m_MaskingEnabled: 0
    m_UnmaskedViews: []
    MaskPreset: {fileID: 0}
  Text:
    m_Untranslated: "In HDRP, the <b>Fog</b> system can be used to simulate denser atmospheres, to increase the perception of depth in the Scene. \n\nThe Fog can react to the lighting to create beautiful volumetric effects, such as sunrays, when using <b>Volumetric Fog,</b> based on a camera frustum voxel technique often called \"froxel\".\n\nLike most other HDRP effects, the Fog can be controlled via a Volume override."
